SUMMARY:Finding Sensitive Data Before Masking: A Human-in-the-Loop Pipelin
 e
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Data Driven\n**Presentation Title:** Finding Sensitive D
 ata Before Masking: A Human-in-the-Loop Pipeline for Enterprise Test Data\
 n\n**Abstract:**\nMost data masking projects begin with a list of columns 
 to transform. But where did that list come from? And what happens when sen
 sitive information is hidden in fields such as notes\, comments\, and free
 -text descriptions?\n\nThis session presents a practical\, human-in-the-lo
 op pipeline for identifying sensitive columns before production data is co
 pied into test environments. The workflow combines column-name and pattern
  signals\, historical masking decisions\, sampled values\, NLP and LLM rev
 iew\, and final analyst approval.\n\nUsing an enterprise Test Data Managem
 ent case study\, I will explain how this approach reduced sensitive-data a
 nalysis time for a medium-sized schema of approximately 100 tables from ab
 out 64 hours to about 2 hours\, while reaching approximately 93% agreement
  with parallel manual review. The session also examines false positives ve
 rsus false negatives\, sample minimization\, responsible API use\, preserv
 ation of data usability\, and the reuse of approved decisions during futur
 e refresh cycles.\n\nThe session is vendor-neutral and uses only synthetic
  examples. Attendees will leave with an implementation blueprint they can 
 adapt to their own data platforms and governance processes.\nAvailable Wee
 k(s)\n\n**Learning Objective:**\nBy the end of this session\, attendees wi
 ll be able to:\n1\\. Design a multi\\-stage pipeline that combines metadat
 a rules\\\, historical decisions\\\, sampled values\\\, NLP/LLM analysis\\
 \, and human review\\.\n2\\. Decide which columns can be classified determ
 inistically and which require value\\-level analysis or analyst escalation
 \\.\n3\\. Evaluate false positives\\\, false negatives\\\, sampling cost\\
 \, and privacy exposure when using AI for sensitive\\-data discovery\\.\n4
 \\. Build a reusable decision repository and feedback loop for future test
 \\-data refresh cycles\\.
